- ALL later steps MUST comply with this baseline.
- NO re-analysis or re-detection of facial landmarks is allowed.

If face detection fails or face is incomplete:
- Abort all beauty, makeup, posture, or geometry-related operations.
- Preserve original face pixels entirely.

---

### SUBJECT POSTURE & ALIGNMENT NORMALIZATION (ID PHOTO COMPLIANCE)

GOAL:
Normalize head, neck, shoulder, and upper-body alignment
to comply with official ID photo standards
WITHOUT altering facial geometry or facial pixels.

ABSOLUTE RULES:
- Facial geometry remains PIXEL-LOCKED.
- Facial pixel region is IMMUNE.
- NO facial feature movement, scaling, warping, interpolation,
  regeneration, or re-synthesis is allowed.

FACE IMMUNITY RULE:
- Face pixels defined during preprocessing MUST NOT be altered,
  re-rendered, resampled, or regenerated.
- All posture corrections must operate OUTSIDE the facial mask.

ALLOWED OPERATIONS (NON-DEFORMATIVE ONLY):
- Canvas-level global rotation of the FULL image.
- Canvas-level translation (X/Y repositioning).
- Uniform scaling ONLY for framing purposes AND
  MUST NOT affect facial pixel density.
- Cropping or canvas re-centering.

FAIL-SAFE:
- Facial identity preservation has ABSOLUTE PRIORITY.
- If posture correction risks ANY facial distortion,
  posture correction MUST be SKIPPED entirely.

---

### ABSOLUTE BIOMETRIC RULES

- FORBIDDEN TO CHANGE facial bone structure, eye sockets, nose shape,
  chin, eyes, eyebrow shape, mouth, or facial proportions.
- FORBIDDEN TO REMOVE moles, scars, freckles, birthmarks,
